cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Cleanplate: Self-Hosted Async Video Watermark Detection, Multi-ROI Inpainting & Automated QA Pipeline"
message: "If you use Cleanplate in your software, media pipeline, or research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/qilaidev/cleanplate"
url: "https://qilaidav.com/workspace/"
abstract: >-
  Cleanplate is an open-source, self-hosted asynchronous video watermark removal and
  overlay inpainting service built on FastAPI, ComfyUI, OpenCV, and FFmpeg. Without
  requiring manual bounding boxes, it performs CFR/SDR ingest normalization, single-pass
  static/translucent OpenCV and ComfyUI native SAM 3.1 segmentation, 16px-aligned
  multi-ROI crop chaining, 81-frame (4k+1) chunked diffusion inpainting with clean-chunk
  GPU bypass, container-aware lossless audio muxing, and automated post-inpaint QA gates
  before delivering clean outputs and structured JSON reports via polling or HMAC-SHA256 webhooks.
authors:
  - name: "qilaidev (qilai Studio)"
    website: "https://qilaidav.com"
keywords:
  - video-watermark-removal
  - watermark-detection
  - video-inpainting
